    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="1240" n="1116" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1116"/>

                <head>No. 674.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 3,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 188.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 330, in reference to the emigration of a pauper whose name is given as
                    Heinrich Ruegger, of Rudolfingen, canton of Zurich, who is represented as now in
                    the poor-house at Ottokee, Ohio; and to commend the intelligence and great zeal
                    you have employed in the investigation of cases like the one you present during
                    a considerable period. The subject of pauper emigration to this country will
                    soon be brought to the attention of Congress.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
